  "body": "## Finding description and impact\n\nThe tokenize function is vulnerable to frontrunning attacks. It allows any user to call the function with a _url parameter and receive ownership or control of a metaCoinAddress associated with that URL. However, the function does not enforce any mechanism to authenticate or prove that the caller is the legitimate owner or originator of the _url. As a result, an attacker can observe a pending transaction attempting to tokenize a specific URL and quickly submit their transaction with a higher gas price to frontrun the original user.\n\nAn attacker can front-run legitimate users and tokenize URLs that do not belong to them. This results in:\n\n* Loss of ownership for the intended user over the tokenized asset.\n* Reputation risk for the platform, as users can lose trust due to the lack of fairness and protection against frontrunning.\n\n## Recommended mitigation steps\n\nConsider using a role-based system to tokenize urls.",
  "proof_of_concept": "pragma solidity 0.8.24;\n\nimport {Test} from \"forge-std/Test.sol\";\nimport {UpsideStakingStub} from \"../contracts/UpsideStakingStub.sol\";\nimport {UpsideProtocol} from \"../contracts/UpsideProtocol.sol\";\nimport {USDCMock} from \"../contracts/mock/USDCMock.sol\";\n\ncontract POC is Test {\n    UpsideStakingStub public stakingStub;\n    UpsideProtocol public upsideProtocol;\n    USDCMock public liquidityToken;\n\n    address public alice;\n    address public bob;\n\n    function setUp() public {\n        stakingStub = new UpsideStakingStub(address(this));\n        stakingStub.setFeeDestinationAddress(address(this));\n\n        liquidityToken = new USDCMock();\n        upsideProtocol = new UpsideProtocol(address(this));\n\n        upsideProtocol.init(address(liquidityToken));   \n        upsideProtocol.setStakingContractAddress(address(stakingStub));\n\n        alice = makeAddr(\"alice\");\n        bob = makeAddr(\"bob\");\n    }\n\n    function test_Frontrun() public {\n        // bob is frontrun by alice\n        \n        vm.prank(alice);\n        address metacoin = upsideProtocol.tokenize(\"https://code4rena.com/\", address(liquidityToken));\n        \n        vm.prank(bob);\n        vm.expectRevert();\n        address metacoin2 = upsideProtocol.tokenize(\"https://code4rena.com/\", address(liquidityToken));\n\n        (address deployer,,,,) = upsideProtocol.metaCoinInfoMap(metacoin);\n        assertEq(deployer, alice, \"Deployer should be Alice\");\n    }\n}",
